---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/recart';
const title = "Recart for Shopify: mobile capture and managed SMS operations";
const desc = "Assess OneClick capture, visitor-to-number identity and the responsibilities behind a managed SMS program.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does OneClick apply to every mobile visitor?",
    "answer": "Recart describes single-tap joining for shoppers with prior Recart popup signup history. Evaluate other visitors and changed-device cases separately."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does managed SMS include all support replies?",
    "answer": "Confirm the reply tooling, service scope, coverage hours and escalation owner in writing; campaign management alone does not establish full customer support coverage."
  },
  {
    "question": "Will my current number and Messenger program transfer automatically?",
    "answer": "Do not assume either. Confirm number release and registration with both providers and obtain explicit current Messenger entitlement for the account."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Operating review · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Where Recart can help</h2>
    <p>The current <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/recart">Recart listing</a> focuses on SMS, email and text list capture, automations and managed service. Reducing mobile form friction and providing an operating partner are useful benefits for a store whose team cannot maintain every campaign itself. They do not establish that captured contacts will produce incremental profit.</p>
    <h2>Understand OneClick eligibility</h2>
    <p>Recart’s <a class="link" href="https://recart.com/">current product site</a> explains that shoppers who previously signed up through a Recart popup can join with a single tap. Evaluate recognized and unrecognized visitors separately. Ask what the shopper sees, which number is selected and how a changed or shared device affects identity. Recognition is a capture mechanism; retain the actual subscription evidence for this store and channel.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise: interrupted capture</h2>
    <p>Use controlled mobile visitors with and without prior recognition. Start capture, dismiss it, return and complete it; then repeat the submission. Inspect the number, disclosure version, timestamp and subscription state in the destination record. Retry after a network interruption and confirm that any welcome is eligible and not duplicated. These are proposed checks, not performed tests or a claim of automatic identity reconciliation.</p>
    <h2>Keep the email handoff explicit</h2>
    <p>Email capture is distinct from SMS delivery. Document which destination receives an email address, which profile keys connect it to the mobile number and how errors are surfaced. A successful popup should not be the only evidence that a destination accepted the record. Leave declined channels declined when updating a returning shopper’s details.</p>
    <h2>Turn managed service into a working brief</h2>
    <p>Recart describes strategy and program assistance on its <a class="link" href="https://recart.com/fully-managed-sms">managed SMS page</a>. Request a written scope: who builds flows, approves copy, verifies offers, updates inventory exclusions and pauses sending during an incident. Give the manager a calendar, eligible audience rules and escalation contacts. Specify an approval deadline and what happens when the merchant cannot approve in time.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise: replies and escalation</h2>
    <p>Ask the team to demonstrate the current reply workflow for your chosen sender and support integration. Send a controlled product question, a complaint and an opt-out request; inspect the handoff, response owner and applicable subscription update. Establish coverage hours, escalation timing and a backup owner. Managed campaign production should not be assumed to include answering every customer conversation.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise: queued cart cancellation</h2>
    <p>Create a cart, let it enter the proposed recovery flow, then purchase before dispatch. Inspect whether the queued reminder is cancelled on the correct profile. Repeat with an order from another device, an opt-out and a refund. Agree which events stop recovery and how delayed Shopify updates are handled. Do not treat attributed cart revenue as evidence that these exit paths work.</p>
    <h2>Confirm number and historical channel continuity</h2>
    <p>Before switching senders, ask both providers about number ownership, release requirements, registration, supported destinations and a feasible cutover window. Keep the existing service until the replacement path is verified; porting is not automatic. Historical Messenger descriptions and the listing’s Messenger integration label do not establish current Messenger sending entitlement. Obtain explicit confirmation if that channel matters to the account.</p>
    <h2>Model fixed commitments before scaling capture</h2>
    <p>Use Recart’s <a class="link" href="https://recart.com/sms-marketing-pricing-ecommerce">current pricing information</a> and an account-specific quote. Separate platform minimums, usage, carrier costs, service scope and setup or overlap costs. More captured numbers can increase spend without improving customer value. Model a low-volume month as well as peak traffic and identify which fixed fees remain when campaigns pause.</p>
    <h2>Judge usable subscribers and incremental contribution</h2>
    <p>For a proposed capture experiment, assign visitors before exposure and track valid, permitted subscriptions per assigned visitor, duplicate records, opt-outs and support effort. Keep assignment stable across return visits. For a sending pilot, compare contribution per assigned eligible contact with a holdout over a defined window: net sales after discounts and refunds less product, fulfillment, message and incremental support costs. Subtract fixed fees separately and avoid deducting the same incentive twice. Require a verified capture path, approved managed brief and tested queue exits before expanding; see <a class="link" href="/guides/list-growth">list growth</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">cost planning</a>.</p>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
